raek@ATHENA.MIT.EDU (Robyn A E Kozierok) writes:


>So, I'm playing a chaotic elf... being chaotic, should I just kill 
>everything in sight, or should I spare friendly monsters?  What
>pleases/pisses off my god?  Recently whenever I offer a corpse it
>says I feel inadequate.  If I get self-knowledge though, it always
>says I am piously aligned.

There are several factors involved in prayer and sacrifice.  There's
alignment, which you increase by killing the right kinds of things.
There's luck, which was recently discussed.  There's the prayer timeout,
which has also been recently talked about.  The god's anger toward 
you is a combination of you luck and alignment.  This appears to be
one of the more complicated parts of the game.

>Oh, while I'm at it, anyone know what controls the seemingly random
>adjustments to your dexterity/wisdom/etc.?

Nethack allows your character to improve himself through exercise!
If you spend a lot of time carrying heavy things your strength will 
go up.  (Don't press this _too_ far though... if you
exert yourself too hard, your con will go down.)  Most of your
basic stats can be improved through exercise, and conversely if
you are stupid you can make them go down too.


